WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:03.420
The Great Debate, Swedenborg vs. Price

00:03.420 --> 00:08.120
Setting. A foggy, candlelit tavern in 1770 London.

00:08.700 --> 00:10.940
The air smells of ale and existential dread.

00:11.540 --> 00:15.000
Emanuel Swedenborg, wild-eyed mystic, sits across from Richard Price,

00:15.300 --> 00:18.780
a bespectacled mathematician clutching a worn copy of Bay's essay.

00:19.540 --> 00:22.720
A crowd of drunk philosophers and curious barmaids leans in,

00:23.140 --> 00:25.180
sensing a brawl of cosmic proportions.

00:27.220 --> 00:29.700
The second coming has dawned Price.

00:30.000 --> 00:31.900
In this very year, 1770,

00:32.380 --> 00:35.780
the Lord has unveiled the spiritual sense of scripture through my pen.

00:36.360 --> 00:37.620
The heavens are open, man.

00:37.940 --> 00:40.560
The new Jerusalem descends and I've seen it with my own eyes,

00:40.820 --> 00:43.720
angels, archetypes, the whole bloody celestial circus.

00:46.140 --> 00:47.960
Price, adjusting his glasses.

00:48.660 --> 00:49.940
Spare me the visions, Emanuel.

00:50.300 --> 00:53.480
Your head's so far in the clouds, you've forgotten how to think on earth.

00:54.320 --> 00:57.660
The real apocalypse hit seven years ago in 1763,

00:57.860 --> 00:59.380
when Bay's Rule saw the light of day.

00:59.960 --> 01:04.860
That little formula, P-H-A-E equals P-E-H-P-H by E,

01:05.260 --> 01:06.820
is the true second coming.

01:07.340 --> 01:09.860
It's not angels singing, it's reason reckoning.

01:10.160 --> 01:10.640
A formula?

01:11.060 --> 01:13.820
You think the divine plan boils down to scribbles on a page?

01:14.360 --> 01:18.380
The Lord's return is a spiritual earthquake, a new dispensation.

01:18.380 --> 01:22.640
I've walked the halls of heaven, Price, while you're playing with numbers like a glorified accountant.

01:23.280 --> 01:23.760
Price.

01:25.040 --> 01:28.760
And I'd rather count truths than chase hallucinations.

01:29.760 --> 01:32.820
Bay's Rule is redemption in action, epistemic salvation.

01:32.820 --> 01:37.820
Humanity's been drowning in dogma, guessing at God's will if it to update our beliefs with evidence.

01:38.300 --> 01:39.540
That's the real New Jerusalem.

01:40.080 --> 01:42.240
A mind that learns, not one that dreams.

01:43.820 --> 01:45.240
Leaning forward, eyes blazing.

01:45.740 --> 01:48.380
You profane the divine with your cold logic.

01:48.380 --> 01:53.360
The second coming is the word-made spirit, not some arithmetic trick.

01:54.100 --> 01:57.780
My heavenly doctrines reveal the inner meaning of scripture, Christ's kingdom within the soul.

01:57.980 --> 02:00.500
Price, sipping his ale, deadpan.

02:01.220 --> 02:01.740
Inner meaning?

02:02.400 --> 02:04.060
Sounds like you're just making it up as you go.

02:04.760 --> 02:06.700
Bay's Rule is the word-made algorithm.

02:07.460 --> 02:09.800
John 1 verse 1 says the Logos was with God.

02:10.380 --> 02:12.020
Well, here it is, in black and white.

02:12.640 --> 02:14.260
Probability as the logic of belief.

02:15.380 --> 02:16.900
Your doctrines are a fever dream.

02:17.400 --> 02:19.320
My equation is a resurrection machine.

02:20.160 --> 02:23.020
Every new datum raises a hypothesis from the dead.

02:23.660 --> 02:24.220
Swedenborg.

02:24.760 --> 02:25.280
Blasphemy.

02:25.740 --> 02:29.520
The last judgment is a cosmic reckoning, not a schoolboy's sum.

02:30.160 --> 02:34.860
In 1770, the spiritual world was reordered, evil cast out, truth enthroned.

02:35.240 --> 02:36.600
What does your precious Bay's do?

02:37.200 --> 02:37.740
Tally bets?

02:38.520 --> 02:39.360
Oh, it's a judgment.

02:39.840 --> 02:40.120
All right.

02:40.120 --> 02:42.400
Bay's sorts the sheep from the goats.

02:42.880 --> 02:44.640
Plausible hypotheses from bullshit.

02:45.040 --> 02:47.260
It's an algorithmic eschatology, Emanuel.

02:47.940 --> 02:52.180
While you're chatting with angels, Bay's is quietly powering every rational mind, every

02:52.180 --> 02:53.740
machine, every scientific leap.

02:54.380 --> 02:55.920
Invisible, yet operative.

02:56.680 --> 02:58.040
Sounds pretty Christ-like to me.

02:59.060 --> 02:59.580
Swedenborg.

03:00.580 --> 03:04.040
You claim your formula is divine, yet it lacks the fire of revelation.

03:04.800 --> 03:06.500
Where is the awe, the mystery?

03:07.260 --> 03:08.600
My visions stir the soul.

03:08.600 --> 03:09.840
Your numbers chill it.

03:11.100 --> 03:11.360
Awe?

03:12.000 --> 03:17.760
Try watching a mind converge on truth, step by step, as priors shift and posteriors solidify.

03:18.260 --> 03:19.140
That's the mystery.

03:19.600 --> 03:22.840
The universe yielding its secrets to a recursive dance of evidence.

03:23.740 --> 03:25.140
Your visions are a one-man show.

03:25.700 --> 03:26.980
Bay's is a universal gospel.

03:26.980 --> 03:30.900
And it started in 1763, not your arbitrary 1770.

03:30.900 --> 03:34.360
Oy, you too?

03:34.360 --> 03:38.700
If this Bay's bloke's so great, why ain't we all praying to probabilities?

03:39.040 --> 03:42.200
And you, Swedenborg, why is your second coming so bloody quiet?

03:42.200 --> 03:44.060
Where's the trumpets?

03:44.060 --> 03:46.800
The trumpets, trumpets are in the heart, my dear.

03:47.280 --> 03:49.900
The Lord works in silence, as do I.

03:50.840 --> 03:55.440
And Bay's works in every decision you make, whether you know it or not.

03:55.440 --> 03:58.980
Next time you bet on a horse, thank 1763.

03:59.760 --> 04:00.200
Fight!

04:01.120 --> 04:01.560
Fight!

04:01.900 --> 04:02.100
Fight!

04:02.540 --> 04:02.820
Fight!

04:03.700 --> 04:05.020
Standing, dramatic as hell.

04:05.460 --> 04:08.140
I'll not brawl with a man who worships fractions.

04:08.700 --> 04:12.240
But mark my words, Price, the Lord's kingdom, is spirit, not sums.

04:12.880 --> 04:13.220
Price.

04:13.900 --> 04:15.580
Also standing, cool as a cucumber.

04:15.920 --> 04:17.500
And I say the kingdom's in the equation.

04:18.060 --> 04:20.020
Bay's is the light, and the light shineth in darkness.

04:21.200 --> 04:21.640
1763.

04:22.280 --> 04:23.540
Mate, deal with it.

04:24.060 --> 04:26.260
They storm out into the fog, coats billowing.

04:26.680 --> 04:28.440
The crowd buzzes with confusion and wonder.

04:28.440 --> 04:30.440
A lone philosopher mutters into his beer.

04:31.880 --> 04:33.860
Maybe they're both right, or both mad.

